Sample pipeline (concrete structure to be adapted to your date ranges):
1) {$addFields: {acqMonth: {$dateToString: {format: "%Y-%m", date: "$acquired_at"}}}}
2) {$bucket: {
    groupBy: "$acqMonth",
    boundaries: ["2022-01","2022-02","2022-03","2022-04","2022-05","2022-06","2022-07"],
    default: "other",
    output: {
      customers: {$push: {id: "$customerId", acquired_at: "$acquired_at", channel: "$channel", product: "$product"}},
      cohort_size: {$sum: 1}
    }
  }}
3) {$project: {cohort: "$_id", cohort_size: 1, customers: 1}}
After obtaining customers per cohort, compute retention by unwinding customers and counting customers having an activity document within 30/60/90 days (you can $lookup into an events collection and $match on event timestamps window, then $group to compute retention rates). Use $facet to produce breakdowns by channel and product within the same aggregation.
